&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;OfferUp is looking for an experienced Senior Sales Account Executive to lead the charge across our Business Verticals (SMB - small to mid sized businesses and B2B) . This role is pivotal in defining our offering for small to mid-size businesses that sell a physical product, such as auto dealerships, furniture stores, appliance retailers, electronics stores, pawn shops, and more. As well as selling a broad range of solutions built to help those businesses hit their marketing goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for a confident self-starter who&#39;s comfortable navigating uncharted territory and wants a real hand in shaping sales strategy for the whole company. We treat every Account Executive like the owner of their own small business: you run your territory, you own your pipeline start to finish, and you bring the hunger to get after it every single day. It&#39;s a grind and it&#39;s genuinely rewarding for the person who wants to build something.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle: prospect, pitch, close, and onboard new customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sell directly to local business owners and operators across high-growth categories including automotive, furniture, appliances, electronics, and specialty retail etc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow your revenue base from a mix of inbound leads and identifying and closing new business through cold outreach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a hunter mentality, proactively research and prospect new business in targeted regions and categories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage a robust pipeline, and forecast new business closure rates and revenue booked&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product, Marketing, and Business Operations so learnings from the field shape OfferUp&#39;s overall direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, track, and report on all prospecting and opportunity stage activity and results in Salesforce.com&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work a hybrid schedule, in the office Tuesdays and Thursdays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
